 126  *A relaxed version of Equation (23a).
 127  vehicle_dynamics_1(i,j,k)$(vehicle_indi(i,j) and k_dynamics(k) ne 0)..           s(i,j,k) - s(i,j,k-1) =g= 0;
 128  vehicle_dynamics_2(i,j,k)$(vehicle_indi(i,j) and k_dynamics(k) ne 0)..           s(i,j,k) - s(i,j,k-1) =l= 26*h*(1-sum(l, p_c(l,k))) + 13*3*sum(l, p_c(l,k));
 129   
      The first constraint ensures vehicles moving forward.
      xThe second constraint essentially penalizes significant changes in position when there are frequent or significant signal phase transitions.
 134   
 135  *A relaxed version of Equation (23b).
 136  car_following(i,j,k)$(vehicle_indi(i,j) and veh_dynamics(i,j) ne 0)..            s(i,j,k) - s(i+1,j,k) =g= vehicle_length(i,j) + minGap(i+1,j)-0.1;
 137  *car_following(i,j,k)$(vehicle_indi(i,j) and veh_dynamics(i,j) ne 0)..            s(i,j,k) - s(i+1,j,k) =g= 3;
